1
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,930
Many road signs are symmetrical.

2
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:15,270
A stop sign is a regular octagon, and a warning sign is often a triangle.

3
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,140
Here is a regular hexagon.

4
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:21,280
All 6 sides are equal, and all 6 angles are equal.

5
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:25,090
How many lines of symmetry does a regular hexagon have?

6
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:28,630
Pause the video and count them.

7
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:31,050
A line of symmetry is a fold line.

8
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:33,880
3 of them join opposite corners.

9
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:36,960
3 more join the middles of opposite sides.

10
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:39,780
That makes 6 lines of symmetry.

11
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:46,820
Remember: in a reflection, every point and its image are the same distance from the mirror line.

12
00:00:46,870 --> 00:00:50,380
The capital letter A has a vertical line of symmetry.

13
00:00:50,430 --> 00:00:54,430
The left half is the mirror image of the right half.

14
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,930
A shape has line symmetry if a line cuts it into two halves that are mirror images.

15
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:03,800
Fold along the line, and the halves match exactly.

16
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:06,190
This T shape has 1 line of symmetry.

17
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,600
We draw it as a dashed line.

18
00:01:08,650 --> 00:01:14,080
A rectangle has 2 lines of symmetry: one vertical and one horizontal.

19
00:01:14,130 --> 00:01:14,770
Your turn.

20
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:18,990
How many lines of symmetry does an equilateral triangle have?

21
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,250
Pause the video and try it.

22
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:26,820
Each line goes from a corner to the middle of the opposite side.

23
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:31,220
There are 3 corners, so there are 3 lines of symmetry.

24
00:01:31,270 --> 00:01:33,520
Now turn a shape about its centre.

25
00:01:33,570 --> 00:01:40,490
A shape has rotational symmetry if it looks exactly the same more than once during a full turn.

26
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:47,180
The order of rotational symmetry is the number of times it looks the same in one full turn.

27
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:49,800
Follow the red corner of this square.

28
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:53,420
After each quarter turn, the square looks the same.

29
00:01:53,470 --> 00:01:56,450
It fits 4 times, so the order is 4.

30
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,140
Your turn.

31
00:01:57,190 --> 00:02:01,010
What is the order of rotational symmetry of a rectangle?

32
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:04,840
Pause the video and think about it.

33
00:02:04,890 --> 00:02:09,580
After a quarter turn, the rectangle stands upright, so it does not fit.

34
00:02:09,630 --> 00:02:11,380
After a half turn, it fits.

35
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:14,140
After a full turn, it fits again.

36
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:16,420
It fits 2 times in a full turn.

37
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:19,770
The order of rotational symmetry is 2.

38
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:24,080
If a shape only fits once, after the full turn, its order is 1.

39
00:02:24,130 --> 00:02:27,170
We say it has no rotational symmetry.

40
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:28,540
Here is the method.

41
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,570
Step 1: look for fold lines.

42
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:34,380
Test vertical, horizontal and diagonal lines.

43
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:41,020
Step 2: turn the shape about its centre, and count how many times it fits in a full turn.

44
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:45,970
Step 3: write both answers: the number of lines, and the order.

45
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:53,660
A useful fact: a regular polygon with n sides has n lines of symmetry, and rotational symmetry of order n.

46
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:57,120
Describe the symmetry of a parallelogram.

47
00:02:57,170 --> 00:02:58,140
Try folding it.

48
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:02,280
No fold line works, because the slanted sides do not line up.

49
00:03:02,330 --> 00:03:04,730
It has no lines of symmetry.

50
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:05,550
Now turn it.

51
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,240
After a half turn, it fits onto itself.

52
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:11,610
So it has rotational symmetry of order 2.

53
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,130
Describe the symmetry of a kite.

54
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:16,210
A kite has 1 line of symmetry.

55
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:20,860
It goes through the two corners where the equal sides meet.

56
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:24,170
No turn fits it onto itself, except a full turn.

57
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:27,610
So the order is 1: no rotational symmetry.

58
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:30,020
2 squares are shaded on this grid.

59
00:03:30,070 --> 00:03:38,170
Shade more squares, so that the pattern has 2 lines of symmetry: the vertical line and the horizontal line.

60
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:42,020
First, reflect each shaded square in the vertical line.

61
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:44,330
That gives 2 new squares.

62
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:48,030
Then reflect all 4 squares in the horizontal line.

63
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,360
That gives 4 more.

64
00:03:49,410 --> 00:03:51,830
We shaded 6 extra squares.

65
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:55,190
How many lines of symmetry does a rectangle have?

66
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,700
Here is Sam's working.

67
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:59,170
Which line goes wrong first?

68
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,270
Line 2 is wrong.

69
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:04,590
Fold a rectangle along a diagonal, and the corners do not meet.

70
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,670
A diagonal is not a line of symmetry.

71
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,570
A rectangle has only 2 lines of symmetry.

72
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:13,240
A square is special: it has 4.

73
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:15,140
Nature is full of symmetry.

74
00:04:15,190 --> 00:04:20,760
A snowflake has 6 lines of symmetry, and rotational symmetry of order 6.

75
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:26,450
Most starfish have 5 arms, so they have rotational symmetry of order 5.

76
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:29,150
And the recycling symbol has 3 arrows.

77
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:34,740
It has rotational symmetry of order 3, but no lines of symmetry at all.

78
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:35,980
One last question.

79
00:04:36,030 --> 00:04:43,920
Which shape has rotational symmetry, but no lines of symmetry: a parallelogram, an isosceles triangle, or a square?

80
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:47,180
Pause the video and answer.

81
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:48,790
It is the parallelogram.

82
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:53,630
It has no fold lines, but it fits onto itself after a half turn.

83
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:56,790
To remember: a line of symmetry is a fold line.

84
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:59,300
The two halves match exactly.

85
00:04:59,350 --> 00:05:05,710
The order of rotational symmetry is the number of times a shape fits in one full turn.

86
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:09,000
Order 1 means no rotational symmetry.

87
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:14,060
A regular polygon with n sides has n lines of symmetry, and order n.

88
00:05:14,110 --> 00:05:19,270
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.1 on Camday.
